LibRaw plug-in for Lumen 1.2
============================

Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export camera raw files: Canon (CR2,
CR3, CRW), Nikon (NEF, NRW), Sony (ARW, SRF, SR2), Fujifilm (RAF),
Olympus (ORF), Panasonic (RW2), Pentax (PEF), Adobe DNG, and the many
other cameras LibRaw 0.22.3 knows.

It is a small program, LumenRaw, which Lumen runs in the background for
each raw file it needs: for a thumbnail it takes the camera's own preview
(quick); for the viewer and exports it develops the raw data with the
camera's white balance and colour matrix, at half size when that is
still big enough (much quicker) and in full for 100% and exports.

It lives in Lumen's Plugins directory (!Lumen.Plugins.LibRaw); PackMan
puts it there. Lumen finds it the next time it starts, and makes the
thumbnails of any raw files that it couldn't before.

The LumenRaw User Guide is in Guide, beside this ReadMe: open
Guide.index/html in a web browser. It explains installing and using the
plug-in and lists every camera it knows (1,181, from LibRaw).

It can also reduce noise on the raw data, before it is made into a
picture (FBDD, and dcraw's wavelet noise reduction), for the photos
that need it: Raw, in the Noise Reduction group of Lumen's Adjustments
tab (Lumen 0.0.38 and later). It is off unless chosen.

Raw files need memory while they are developed: a 24 megapixel one takes
about 300 MB for a few seconds.

